§§ `Hand-written cases: exact words of a charge`

-- s 311, infanticide
`Infanticide by a mother after birth` MEANS `Infanticide Facts` WITH
    `particulars` IS `the particulars`
    `victim` IS "Baby Lim"
    `victim described as` IS ""
    `the manner` IS "by smothering the said child"
    `the accused is a woman` IS TRUE
    `by an intentional act or omission causes the death of her child` IS TRUE
    `the child is below 12 months of age` IS TRUE
    `the balance of her mind was disturbed by reason of her not having fully recovered from the effect of giving birth to the child` IS TRUE
    `the balance of her mind was disturbed by reason of the effect of lactation consequent upon the birth of the child` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `offence under s 311` `Infanticide by a mother after birth`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 311` `Infanticide by a mother after birth`)'s `made out`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 311` `Infanticide by a mother after birth`)'s section EQUALS "311"
#ASSERT (`charge under s 311` `Infanticide by a mother after birth`)'s offence EQUALS "infanticide"
#ASSERT (`charge under s 311` `Infanticide by a mother after birth`)'s punishment EQUALS "imprisonment for life, or with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall, if she is not sentenced to imprisonment for life, also be liable to fine"
#ASSERT (`charge under s 311` `Infanticide by a mother after birth`)'s text EQUALS "You, Tan Ah Kow, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of March 2025, at about 9.30 pm, at Block 123 Ang Mo Kio Avenue 3, Singapore, did, being a woman, by an intentional act or omission cause the death of her child, one Baby Lim, a child below 12 months of age, at a time when the balance of your mind was disturbed by reason of the effect of giving birth to the said child or of lactation, and thereby commit the offence of infanticide, to wit, by smothering the said child, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 311 of the Penal Code 1871."
-- s 310: the child is below 12 months; at 12 months it is not (the helper's line)
#ASSERT `below 12 months of age` 11
#ASSERT NOT (`below 12 months of age` 12)
-- s 310 does not make "murder but for this section" an element ("notwithstanding that ..."): the ladder asks only for the woman, the act, the child and the disturbance
-- s 304C(4), by the accused's own act
`Household death by A's own act` MEANS `Household Death Facts` WITH
    `particulars` IS `the particulars`
    `victim` IS "Lim Mei Ling"
    `victim described as` IS ""
    `the manner` IS "by striking the said child repeatedly"
    `B is below 14 years of age` IS TRUE
    `B is a domestic worker` IS FALSE
    `B is a vulnerable person` IS FALSE
    `B dies as a result of an unlawful act` IS TRUE
    `the person who did that act was a member of the same household as B` IS TRUE
    `the person who did that act had frequent contact with B` IS TRUE
    `A was a member of the same household as B` IS TRUE
    `A had frequent contact with B at the time of that act` IS TRUE
    `at that time there was a significant risk of grievous hurt being caused to B by the unlawful act of such a person` IS TRUE
    `A was the person whose act caused B's death` IS TRUE
    `A was, or ought to have been, aware of the significant risk` IS FALSE
    `A failed to take such steps as A could reasonably have been expected to take to protect B from the significant risk` IS FALSE
    `the unlawful act occurred in circumstances of the kind that A foresaw or ought to have foreseen` IS FALSE
    `A could not have been expected in A's circumstances to take any such step` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `offence under s 304C(4)` `Household death by A's own act`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 304C(4)` `Household death by A's own act`)'s text EQUALS "You, Tan Ah Kow, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of March 2025, at about 9.30 pm, at Block 123 Ang Mo Kio Avenue 3, Singapore, being a member of the same household as one Lim Mei Ling and having frequent contact with the said person, did by your own unlawful act cause the death of the said person, to wit, by striking the said child repeatedly, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 304C(4) of the Penal Code 1871."
-- s 304C(4), by failing to protect (the second alternative of (1)(d))
`Household death by A's failure to protect` MEANS `Household Death Facts` WITH
    `particulars` IS `the particulars`
    `victim` IS "Lim Mei Ling"
    `victim described as` IS ""
    `the manner` IS "by failing to protect the said child from repeated assaults by another member of the household"
    `B is below 14 years of age` IS TRUE
    `B is a domestic worker` IS FALSE
    `B is a vulnerable person` IS FALSE
    `B dies as a result of an unlawful act` IS TRUE
    `the person who did that act was a member of the same household as B` IS TRUE
    `the person who did that act had frequent contact with B` IS TRUE
    `A was a member of the same household as B` IS TRUE
    `A had frequent contact with B at the time of that act` IS TRUE
    `at that time there was a significant risk of grievous hurt being caused to B by the unlawful act of such a person` IS TRUE
    `A was the person whose act caused B's death` IS FALSE
    `A was, or ought to have been, aware of the significant risk` IS TRUE
    `A failed to take such steps as A could reasonably have been expected to take to protect B from the significant risk` IS TRUE
    `the unlawful act occurred in circumstances of the kind that A foresaw or ought to have foreseen` IS TRUE
    `A could not have been expected in A's circumstances to take any such step` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `offence under s 304C(4)` `Household death by A's failure to protect`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 304C(4)` `Household death by A's failure to protect`)'s text EQUALS "You, Tan Ah Kow, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of March 2025, at about 9.30 pm, at Block 123 Ang Mo Kio Avenue 3, Singapore, being a member of the same household as one Lim Mei Ling and having frequent contact with the said person, did fail to take such steps as you could reasonably have been expected to take to protect the said person from a significant risk of grievous hurt, whereby the said person died as a result of the unlawful act of a member of the same household, to wit, by failing to protect the said child from repeated assaults by another member of the household, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 304C(4) of the Penal Code 1871."
-- s 304C(3): "A is not guilty of an offence under this section if A could not have been expected in A's circumstances to take any such step"
-- (the first alternative is by A's own act: step-taking is not in question there; the flat negative reading applies to the whole offence: FORK DEF-A4)
`Household death, failure to protect, A could not have been expected to act` MEANS `Household Death Facts` WITH
    `particulars` IS `the particulars`
    `victim` IS "Lim Mei Ling"
    `victim described as` IS ""
    `the manner` IS "by failing to protect the said child"
    `B is below 14 years of age` IS TRUE
    `B is a domestic worker` IS FALSE
    `B is a vulnerable person` IS FALSE
    `B dies as a result of an unlawful act` IS TRUE
    `the person who did that act was a member of the same household as B` IS TRUE
    `the person who did that act had frequent contact with B` IS TRUE
    `A was a member of the same household as B` IS TRUE
    `A had frequent contact with B at the time of that act` IS TRUE
    `at that time there was a significant risk of grievous hurt being caused to B by the unlawful act of such a person` IS TRUE
    `A was the person whose act caused B's death` IS FALSE
    `A was, or ought to have been, aware of the significant risk` IS TRUE
    `A failed to take such steps as A could reasonably have been expected to take to protect B from the significant risk` IS TRUE
    `the unlawful act occurred in circumstances of the kind that A foresaw or ought to have foreseen` IS TRUE
    `A could not have been expected in A's circumstances to take any such step` IS TRUE

#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 304C(4)` `Household death, failure to protect, A could not have been expected to act`)
#ASSERT NOT (`charge under s 304C(4)` `Household death, failure to protect, A could not have been expected to act`)'s `made out`
-- s 304C(2): the prosecution need not prove which alternative of (1)(d) applies: both together make the offence out too
`Household death, both alternatives of (1)(d)` MEANS `Household Death Facts` WITH
    `particulars` IS `the particulars`
    `victim` IS "Lim Mei Ling"
    `victim described as` IS ""
