#ASSERT `s 304C(5)(c) the act is unlawful` `Unlawful, an offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 304C(5)(c) the act is unlawful` `Unlawful, by a child below the age in section 82` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 304C(5)(c) the act is unlawful` `Unlawful, by a person of the age in section 83 without sufficient maturity` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 304C(5)(c) the act is unlawful` `Unlawful, by a person of unsound mind` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 304C(5)(c) the act is unlawful` `Unlawful, by an intoxicated person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 304C(5)(c) the act is unlawful` `Unlawful, by a person who made a mistake of fact` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an act by A himself is outside the definition ("other than an act by A"): the text does not say what makes it unlawful (NOTHING-kind)
#ASSERT `s 304C(5)(c) the act is unlawful` `Unlawful, an act of A` EQUALS NOTHING
-- an act that is none of these: the definition says "is one that ...", read as closed (marginal reading a)
#ASSERT `s 304C(5)(c) the act is unlawful` `Unlawful, none of these` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 335A(3): the same shape
#ASSERT `s 335A(3) the act is unlawful` `Unlawful, an offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 335A(3) the act is unlawful` `Unlawful, by a child below the age in section 82` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 335A(3) the act is unlawful` `Unlawful, by a person of the age in section 83 without sufficient maturity` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 335A(3) the act is unlawful` `Unlawful, by a person of unsound mind` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 335A(3) the act is unlawful` `Unlawful, by an intoxicated person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 335A(3) the act is unlawful` `Unlawful, by a person who made a mistake of fact` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 335A(3) the act is unlawful` `Unlawful, an act of A` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 335A(3) the act is unlawful` `Unlawful, none of these` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 304C(5)(a): a person who does not live in the household is regarded as a member "if that person visits it so often and for such periods of time that it is reasonable"
-- a rule that adds members, so a person who does not meet it is not said to be a non-member (NOTHING-kind)
#ASSERT `s 304C(5)(a) the person who does not live in the household is a member of it` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 304C(5)(a) the person who does not live in the household is a member of it` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 304C(5)(b): where B lived in different households at different times, "the same household as B" is the one in which B was living at the time of the act
#ASSERT `s 304C(5)(b) the household is the same household as B` "the household at 12 Jalan Besar" "the household at 12 Jalan Besar" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 304C(5)(b) the household is the same household as B` "the household at 12 Jalan Besar" "the household at 7 Bedok Road" EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 304C(5)(e) and s 335A(4): A's circumstances "include but is not limited to" those experiences
#ASSERT `s 304C(5)(e) the circumstance is among A's circumstances` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 304C(5)(e) the circumstance is among A's circumstances` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 335A(4) the circumstance is among A's circumstances` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 335A(4) the circumstance is among A's circumstances` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 335A(6): "sexual abuse" means abuse caused to a victim by the commission of a sexual offence within the meaning of section 2(1) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010: a "means" definition
#ASSERT `s 335A(6) the abuse is sexual abuse` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 335A(6) the abuse is sexual abuse` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 315(2) - the length of a pregnancy`

-- "evidence that a woman had at any material time been pregnant for a period of 28 weeks or more shall be prima facie evidence that she was at that time pregnant of a child capable of being born alive"
#ASSERT NOT (`28 weeks or more` 27)
#ASSERT `28 weeks or more` 28
#ASSERT `28 weeks or more` 40
#ASSERT `s 315(2) the effect of evidence of the length of the pregnancy` 28 EQUALS `prima facie evidence that she was pregnant of a child capable of being born alive`
#ASSERT `s 315(2) the effect of evidence of the length of the pregnancy` 36 EQUALS `prima facie evidence that she was pregnant of a child capable of being born alive`
-- a shorter pregnancy: the subsection says nothing (a presumption limited by its own wording: NOTHING-kind, not "the child was not capable of being born alive")
#ASSERT `s 315(2) the effect of evidence of the length of the pregnancy` 27 EQUALS `not covered by s 315(2)`
#ASSERT `s 315(2) the effect of evidence of the length of the pregnancy` 0 EQUALS `not covered by s 315(2)`

§§ `s 316 - the hypothetical act, and the Illustration`

-- the hypothetical leaf is set from `commits culpable homicide` on the facts of the same act with the death caused (the module's comment says so)
-- Illustration: "A, knowing that he is likely to cause the death of a pregnant woman, does an act which, if it caused the death of the woman, would amount to culpable homicide.
-- The woman is injured, but does not die; but the death of an unborn quick child with which she is pregnant is thereby caused. A is guilty of the offence defined in this section."
`A would be guilty of culpable homicide had the woman died` MEANS `Homicide Facts` WITH
    `particulars` IS `the particulars`
    `victim` IS "the woman"
    `victim described as` IS ""
    `the manner` IS "by striking the said woman in the abdomen with an iron bar"
    `causes death by doing an act` IS TRUE
    `with the intention of causing death` IS FALSE
    `with the intention of causing such bodily injury as is likely to cause death` IS FALSE
    `with the knowledge that he is likely by such act to cause death` IS TRUE
    `with the intention of causing such bodily injury as the offender knows to be likely to cause the death of the person to whom the harm is caused` IS FALSE
    `with the intention of causing bodily injury to any person` IS FALSE
    `the bodily injury intended to be inflicted is sufficient in the ordinary course of nature to cause death` IS FALSE
    `knows that the act is so imminently dangerous that it must in all probability cause death, or such bodily injury as is likely to cause death` IS FALSE
    `commits such act without any excuse for incurring the risk of causing death or such injury` IS FALSE
    `whilst deprived of the power of self-control by grave and sudden provocation` IS FALSE
    `causes the death of the person who gave the provocation, or of any other person by mistake or accident` IS FALSE
    `the provocation is not sought or voluntarily provoked by the offender as an excuse for killing or doing harm to any person` IS FALSE
    `the offender did not know and had no reason to believe that the provocation was given by anything done in obedience to the law, or by a public servant in the lawful exercise of his powers` IS FALSE
    `the provocation is not given by anything done in the lawful exercise of the right of private defence` IS FALSE
    `private defence` IS `no private defence`
    `causes the death of the person against whom he is exercising such right of defence` IS FALSE
    `without premeditation formed prior to the circumstances which gave rise to the act of private defence` IS FALSE
    `without any intention of doing more harm than is necessary for the purpose of such defence` IS FALSE
    `being a public servant, or aiding a public servant acting for the advancement of public justice, exceeds the powers given to him by law` IS FALSE
    `causes death by doing an act which he, in good faith, believes to be lawful and necessary for the due discharge of his duty as such public servant` IS FALSE
    `without ill will towards the person whose death is caused` IS FALSE
    `without premeditation formed prior to the circumstances constituting the sudden fight` IS FALSE
    `in a sudden fight` IS FALSE
    `in the heat of passion upon a sudden quarrel` IS FALSE
    `without the offender having taken undue advantage or acted in a cruel or unusual manner` IS FALSE
    `the offender did not know and had no reason to believe that the person whose death was caused was acting in obedience to the law, or was a public servant acting in the lawful exercise of his powers` IS FALSE
    `the person whose death is caused is above 18 years of age` IS FALSE
    `suffers death or takes the risk of death with his own consent` IS FALSE
    `the offender being a woman voluntarily causes the death of her child` IS FALSE
    `the child is below 12 months of age` IS FALSE
    `the balance of her mind was disturbed by reason of her not having fully recovered from the effect of giving birth to the child or by reason of the effect of lactation` IS FALSE
    `the offender was suffering from an abnormality of mind` IS FALSE
    `the abnormality of mind arose from a condition of arrested or retarded development or any inherent causes, or was induced by disease or injury` IS FALSE
    `the abnormality of mind substantially impaired his capacity to know the nature of the acts or omissions` IS FALSE
    `substantially impaired capacity to know that the acts or omissions are wrong by the ordinary standards of reasonable and honest persons` IS FALSE
    `substantially impaired capacity to know that the acts or omissions are wrong as contrary to law` IS FALSE
    `the abnormality of mind substantially impaired his power to control his acts or omissions` IS FALSE
    `under such circumstances that if he by that act caused death he would be guilty of murder` IS FALSE
    `under such circumstances that if he by that act caused death he would be guilty of culpable homicide not amounting to murder` IS FALSE
    `hurt is caused to any person by such act` IS FALSE
    `under sentence of imprisonment for life` IS FALSE

`no private defence` MEANS `Private Defence Facts` WITH
    `the act was done in defence against the act giving rise to the right` IS FALSE
