§§ `s 335A - allowing neglect, hurt or abuse`

-- s 335A(5): death is not an element, it chooses the punishment (a) where death is caused, 7 years or fine up to $20,000 or both; (b) in any other case, 4 years or fine up to $4,000 or both
`Allowing neglect of a domestic worker, no death` MEANS `Allowing Neglect Facts` WITH
    `particulars` IS `the particulars`
    `victim` IS "Lim Mei Ling"
    `victim described as` IS ""
    `the manner` IS "by failing to report that the employer's son was repeatedly striking the said domestic worker"
    `B is a domestic worker` IS TRUE
    `B is a vulnerable person` IS FALSE
    `B suffers neglect, hurt, grievous hurt, sexual abuse or any injury to B's mental health as a result of the unlawful act of another person (C)` IS TRUE
    `A knew or had reason to believe that B was at risk of such neglect, hurt, grievous hurt, sexual abuse or injury caused by C` IS TRUE
    `A was at the time of the risk the employer of B, a member of B's employer's household or an employment agent of B` IS TRUE
    `A had, at the time of the risk, the custody, charge or care of B` IS FALSE
    `A failed to take such steps as A could reasonably have been expected to take in A's circumstances to protect B from the risk` IS TRUE
    `the act occurred in circumstances of the kind that A foresaw or ought to have foreseen` IS TRUE
    `death is caused to the domestic worker or vulnerable person` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `offence under s 335A(1)` `Allowing neglect of a domestic worker, no death`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 335A(1)` `Allowing neglect of a domestic worker, no death`)'s punishment EQUALS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 4 years, or with fine which may extend to $4,000, or with both"
#ASSERT (`charge under s 335A(1)` `Allowing neglect of a domestic worker, no death`)'s text EQUALS "You, Tan Ah Kow, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of March 2025, at about 9.30 pm, at Block 123 Ang Mo Kio Avenue 3, Singapore, being the employer of one Lim Mei Ling, a domestic worker, a member of the employer's household or an employment agent of the said domestic worker, knowing or having reason to believe that the said domestic worker was at risk of neglect, hurt, grievous hurt, sexual abuse or injury to mental health caused by another person, did fail to take such steps as you could reasonably have been expected to take in your circumstances to protect the said domestic worker from that risk, whereby the said domestic worker suffered such harm as a result of the unlawful act of that person, in circumstances of the kind that you foresaw or ought to have foreseen, to wit, by failing to report that the employer's son was repeatedly striking the said domestic worker, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 335A(1) of the Penal Code 1871."
`Allowing neglect of a vulnerable person, death caused` MEANS `Allowing Neglect Facts` WITH
    `particulars` IS `the particulars`
    `victim` IS "Lim Mei Ling"
    `victim described as` IS ""
    `the manner` IS "by leaving the said person in the care of a known abuser"
    `B is a domestic worker` IS FALSE
    `B is a vulnerable person` IS TRUE
    `B suffers neglect, hurt, grievous hurt, sexual abuse or any injury to B's mental health as a result of the unlawful act of another person (C)` IS TRUE
    `A knew or had reason to believe that B was at risk of such neglect, hurt, grievous hurt, sexual abuse or injury caused by C` IS TRUE
    `A was at the time of the risk the employer of B, a member of B's employer's household or an employment agent of B` IS FALSE
    `A had, at the time of the risk, the custody, charge or care of B` IS TRUE
    `A failed to take such steps as A could reasonably have been expected to take in A's circumstances to protect B from the risk` IS TRUE
    `the act occurred in circumstances of the kind that A foresaw or ought to have foreseen` IS TRUE
    `death is caused to the domestic worker or vulnerable person` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `offence under s 335A(2)` `Allowing neglect of a vulnerable person, death caused`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 335A(2)` `Allowing neglect of a vulnerable person, death caused`)'s punishment EQUALS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, or with fine which may extend to $20,000, or with both"
-- the two subsections are different offences: (1) needs a domestic worker and (2) a vulnerable person
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 335A(1)` `Allowing neglect of a vulnerable person, death caused`)
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 335A(2)` `Allowing neglect of a domestic worker, no death`)
